{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-42497","model_call":11,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1476"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1476"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_20_1076942216#1_2357662744","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1476","rank":2,"snippet":"Action About the Author: Rebecca Pryor Other Contributors: \" , \"segment\": \"With our tendency to just throw away products and continually purchase new ones, this creates a global e-waste problem. E-Waste’s Impact on the Environment Image by George Hotelling from Canton, MI, United States (E-waste recycling in Ann Arbor) [ CC BY-SA 2.0 ], via Wikimedia Commons The environmental hazards caused by improper disposal of <cover>e-waste can be briefly described as follows: Air Pollution: Burning of wires release hydrocarbons in the atmosphere. Water Pollution: Electronic devices contain toxic metals like mercury, lead and lithium, which when disposed of improperly, mixes with ponds, lakes and groundwater. Communities that directly depend on these sources of water then consume it unknowingly. These heavy metals </cover>are hazardous for all forms of living beings. Soil Pollution: These heavy metals enter the food chain as they are absorbed by plants from the soil.\" , \"start_char\": 390.000000 , \"title\": \"How to Reduce Electronic Waste (E-Waste): 10 Simple Tips\" , \"url\": \"https://get-green-now.com/reduce-ewaste-hazards/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_34_1636826970#2_3436850066","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":6},"model_calls":11,"document_judgments":8,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
