{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-42497","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"informal sector\" \"informal recycling\" \"primitive recycling\" backyard) (+ \"e-waste\" \"electronic waste\") (+ \"open burning\" combustion incineration) (+ \"particulate matter\" dioxins furans \"heavy metals\" \"air pollution\"))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"informal sector\" \"informal recycling\" \"primitive recycling\" backyard) (+ \"e-waste\" \"electronic waste\") (+ \"open burning\" combustion incineration) (+ \"particulate matter\" dioxins furans \"heavy metals\" \"air pollution\"))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1276221077#0_2305273239","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1482","rank":1,"snippet":"China, India, Pakistan, Vietnam, and the Philippines handle anywhere from 50 percent to 80 percent of this e-waste, often shredding, burning, and dismantling the products in “backyards.” Emissions from these recycling practices are damaging human health and the environment. 2 Developing countries with rapidly growing economies handle e-waste from developed countries, and from their own internal consumers. Currently, an estimated 70 percent of e-waste handled in India is from other nations, but the UNEP estimates that between 2007 and 2020, domestic television e-waste will double, computer e-waste will increase five times, and cell phones 18 times. The <cover>informal sector’s recycling practices magnify health risks. For example, primary and secondary exposure to toxic metals, such as lead, results mainly from open-air burning used to retrieve valuable components such as gold. Combustion from burning e-waste creates fine particulate matter, </cover>which is linked to pulmonary and cardiovascular disease.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"The Human and Environmental Effects of E-Waste – Population Reference Bureau\" , \"url\": \"http://www.prb.org/Publications/Articles/2013/e-waste.aspx\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1276221077#0_2305273239","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":434},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":25,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-42497","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1482"},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":25,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-42497","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1482"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1482"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1276221077#1_2305275296","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1482","rank":2,"snippet":"Effects of E-Waste References Date Authors Lucy McAllister \" , \"segment\": \"2 Developing countries with rapidly growing economies handle e-waste from developed countries, and from their own internal consumers. Currently, an estimated 70 percent of e-waste handled in India is from other nations, but the UNEP estimates that between 2007 and 2020, domestic television e-waste will double, computer e-waste will increase five times, and cell phones 18 times. The <cover>informal sector’s recycling practices magnify health risks. For example, primary and secondary exposure to toxic metals, such as lead, results mainly from open-air burning used to retrieve valuable components such as gold. Combustion from burning e-waste creates fine particulate matter, </cover>which is linked to pulmonary and cardiovascular disease. While the health implications of e-waste are difficult to isolate due to the informal working conditions, poverty, and poor sanitation, several studies in Guiyu, a city in southeastern China, offer insight. Guiyu is known as the largest e-waste recycling site in the world, and the city’s residents exhibit substantial digestive, neurological, respiratory, and bone problems. For example, 80 percent of Guiyu’s children experience respiratory ailments, and are ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1276221077#1_2305275296","rank":2,"relevance":3}]},"time":1},"model_calls":34,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":25,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
