{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-42497","model_call":34,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1482"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1482"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_26_1721682000#17_2990568532","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1482","rank":6,"snippet":"which the physical spread of (urban) development across the landscape far outpaces population growth.\" urban sprawl ________ is defined as liquid that leaks from sanitary landfills when substances in waste dissolve in water as rainwater percolates downward. Leachate What is a consequence of the NIMBY syndrome when talking about building a new landfill in an area? People in most communities do not want a landfill located \"in their <cover>backyard,\" so it is hard to find suitable areas for new landfills. Which of the following is not a potential characteristic of hazardous waste? -toxic -chemically reactive -flammable -corrosive Why is electronic waste such as televisions, computers, and cell phones (\"e-waste\") classified as hazardous waste? It contains large amounts of heavy metals (lead, cadmium, mercury). Which of the following is a drawback of combustion? -</cover>Incineration produces air pollution -Incineration can produce offensive odors -These facilities are expensive to build -Combustion ash is often toxic and must be disposed of in specific landfills In the United States, what three things comprise the principal components of municipal solid waste? Paper, food scraps, and yard trimmings What does the U.S. Resource Conservation and Recovery Act (RCRA) address?\" , \"start_char\":","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1276221077#0_2305273239","rank":1,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_08_1276221077#1_2305275296","rank":2,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_17_458328791#6_496702648","rank":3,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1690664467#4_3248127945","rank":4,"relevance":3},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1