{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-42497","model_call":59,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1500"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1500"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_291506052#16_666141079","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1500","rank":2,"snippet":"7 – 750 Words) What Is Air Pollution? Causes of Air Pollution: Effects of Air Pollution: How can we stop Air Pollution? Conclusion: Essay on Air Pollution in India – Causes, Effects and Prevention (Essay 8 – 1000 Words) Introduction: Causes of Air Pollution in India: Effects of Air Pollution: Prevention of Air Pollution in India: Conclusion: Essay on Air Pollution in India – For Civil Services, IAS, IPS, UPSC and Other Competitive Exams (Essay 9 – 1500 Words) Introduction: Causes: Effects: Control: Air Pollution in <cover>India: Conclusion: Like this post? Don’t forget to share it! \" , \"segment\": \"Waste Disposal: Disposal of wastes, whether biological, plastic or e-waste, without proper treatment, also contribute to air pollution. Burning </cover>plastic will produce many harmful gases, which will be a threat to the surrounding atmosphere and cause serious breathing problem in people. This applies to e-wastes too. Biological wastes while decomposition releases the foul smell. Disposal of waste in an authorized manner is an important task. 4. Cutting Trees or Deforestation: Green leaves absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere during days to produce food using the process photosynthesis. This process helps the atmosphere to maintain its balance with gaseous compositions.","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_19_1082813673#4_1510636196","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":6},"model_calls":59,"document_judgments":47,"relevance_3":29,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
